*** collect() method in Streams ***

--> collect() is a terminal operation
--> It converts a Stream into some result
--> The logic of how to collect is defined by a Collector

Example :
List<Integer> list =  stream.collect(Collectors.toList());

Flow :
Stream → collect() → Collector → Final Result

Example result types:
List
Set
Map
String
Grouping
Partitioning
Statistics


Stream processes elements but does not store them. collect() is the way to materialize the result.

*** What is Collectors? ****

Collectors is simply a utility class that provides ready-made Collector implementations.

Example methods :

toList()
toSet()
toMap()
groupingBy()
partitioningBy()
joining()
counting()
averagingInt()


Example :
List<Integer> list = stream.collect(Collectors.toList());

*** groupingBy() ***

groupingBy() is used when we want to:
    1. Group elements based on a property
    2. The result of groupingBy() is always a Map.


























